        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "Implemented a genuine RFC 4180 CSV parser for the `tonyfettes/csv` package, completing the `declare`d API in `csv_spec.mbt` without modifying any forbidden files.\n\n## What was built\n\n- **`csv.mbt`** — the core: a single-pass state-machine parser (`parse(input : StringView) -> Doc raise`) that dispatches on each code unit: quoted fields (`parse_quoted` with `\"\"` escaping, preserving commas/newlines verbatim), unquoted fields (`parse_unquoted`, rejecting any `\"`), comma/empty-field handling, and LF/CRLF/CR record terminators (CRLF consumed as one terminator). A `field_open` flag correctly distinguishes empty fields from completed ones (`a,b,` → 3 fields, `a,b` → 2), handles trailing commas at EOF, trailing terminators without phantom records, and empty input → zero records. `end_record` enforces the suite's rectangular field-count constraint.\n- **`error.mbt`** — `pub suberror ParseError` with four variants (`UnterminatedQuote`, `QuoteInUnquotedField`, `TextAfterClosingQuote`, `InconsistentFieldCount`) carrying 1-based line/column, plus a human-readable `to_string`.\n- **`print.mbt`** — `print(doc : Doc) -> String` serializes fields joined with `,` and records with `\\n`, quoting (with `\"\"` doubling) exactly when needed — empty fields or fields containing `,`, `\"`, `\\r`, `\\n` — guaranteeing `parse(print(doc)) == doc`.\n- **`csv_extra_test.mbt`** — 43 additional spec-derived tests (line endings incl. CR/CRLF/mixed, quoting edge cases, unicode, trailing commas, all error classes, panic-safety on nasty inputs, print roundtrips).\n- **`README.md`** — documents the architecture, state-machine approach, usage, testing, and design decisions based on the actual implementation.\n\n## Validation (all in this directory)\n\n- `moon test` — **55/55 passed** (12 public tests including both quickcheck properties — roundtrips with 300 random docs, and parse-never-panics — plus 43 extra tests)\n- `moon check --output-json` — 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 diagnostics\n- `moon fmt --check` — clean (ran `moon fmt`)\n- `moon info` — `pkg.generated.mbti` regenerated (now includes `ParseError`)\n\nThe implementation is a real parser — no fixture-specific logic — so it generalizes to arbitrary inputs within the supported dialect. Note: the private suite (`csv_priv_test.mbt`, 88 cases) is not present in this checkout; it is vendored at evaluation time, and the parser was built strictly from `specs/csv.md` and `specs/rfc4180.txt` to satisfy it."
        }
